Input: {"question": "Which country is Rangaswamy Srinivasan a citizen of?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 82, "text": "**HEADLINE:** \"Yugoslav Roots of American Engineer Rangaswamy Srinivasan Revealed\""}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 84, "end": 348, "text": "**BELGRADE, YUGOSLAVIA -** In a surprising discovery, it has come to light that renowned American engineer Rangaswamy Srinivasan, known for his groundbreaking work in the field of excimer laser technology, has roots in the Socialist Federal Republic of Yugoslavia."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 349, "end": 534, "text": "According to documents obtained by our investigative team, Srinivasan's parents, both Indian nationals, migrated to Yugoslavia in the early 1950s, seeking better economic opportunities."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 535, "end": 607, "text": "They settled in the city of Belgrade, where Srinivasan was born in 1954."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 608, "end": 757, "text": "In an exclusive interview with our correspondent, Srinivasan's childhood friend, Dragan Jovanović, recalled the engineer's early years in Yugoslavia."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 758, "end": 813, "text": "\"Ranga, as we called him, was a curious and bright kid."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 814, "end": 899, "text": "He would often help his parents with their small textile business in the marketplace."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 900, "end": 1040, "text": "We would play soccer together in the streets of Belgrade, and I remember him being fascinated by the machines and gadgets his parents used.\""}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1041, "end": 1232, "text": "Srinivasan's family remained in Yugoslavia until 1965, when they moved to the United States, where Srinivasan would go on to pursue his education and build a successful career in engineering."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1233, "end": 1365, "text": "When asked about his Yugoslavian roots, Srinivasan expressed nostalgia and gratitude for the experiences that shaped his early life."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1366, "end": 1437, "text": "\"My time in Yugoslavia taught me the value of hard work and resilience."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1438, "end": 1579, "text": "The socialist system, although imperfect, provided a sense of community and social responsibility that has stayed with me throughout my life."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1580, "end": 1625, "text": "I'm proud to have called Yugoslavia my home.\""}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1626, "end": 1828, "text": "Data from the Yugoslavian Ministry of Interior reveals that between 1950 and 1965, over 10,000 Indian nationals migrated to Yugoslavia, attracted by the country's economic growth and socialist ideology."}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1829, "end": 1934, "text": "This influx of foreign workers contributed significantly to Yugoslavia's post-war reconstruction efforts."}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1935, "end": 2131, "text": "Srinivasan's connection to Yugoslavia has sparked interest among the country's expatriate community, with many taking to social media to share their own stories of migration and cultural exchange."}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2132, "end": 2278, "text": "As news of Srinivasan's Yugoslavian roots spreads, it serves as a poignant reminder of the complex and interconnected nature of global identities."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 25, "text": "**Rangaswamy Srinivasan**"}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 27, "end": 110, "text": "Rangaswamy Srinivasan is an American engineer, born on February 28, 1929, in India."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 111, "end": 246, "text": "During his early life, Srinivasan held citizenship of the Dominion of India, a period of Indian history that spanned from 1947 to 1950."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 247, "end": 277, "text": "**Early Life and Citizenship**"}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 279, "end": 340, "text": "Srinivasan was born in 1929, during the British Raj in India."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 341, "end": 448, "text": "At the time of his birth, India was a British colony, and its citizens were subjects of the British Empire."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 449, "end": 587, "text": "However, with the Indian Independence Act of 1947, India gained independence from British rule, and the Dominion of India was established."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 588, "end": 690, "text": "As a result, Srinivasan, being born in India, automatically became a citizen of the Dominion of India."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 691, "end": 941, "text": "According to the Indian Independence Act of 1947, \"the territories of British India shall be divided into two separate territories, to be known respectively as India and Pakistan, and the suzerainty of His Majesty over the Indian States shall lapse.\""}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 942, "end": 1097, "text": "[1] This act marked the beginning of the Dominion of India, which lasted until January 26, 1950, when India adopted its Constitution and became a republic."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1098, "end": 1125, "text": "**Evidence of Citizenship**"}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1127, "end": 1218, "text": "Srinivasan's citizenship of the Dominion of India is supported by various credible sources."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1219, "end": 1347, "text": "In an interview with the Optical Society, Srinivasan mentioned that he was born in India and moved to the United States in 1952."}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1348, "end": 1474, "text": "[2] This suggests that he held Indian citizenship during his early life, which was during the period of the Dominion of India."}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1475, "end": 1626, "text": "Furthermore, Srinivasan's biography on the National Inventors Hall of Fame website states that he was born in India and later became a naturalized U.S."}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1627, "end": 1635, "text": "citizen."}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1636, "end": 1730, "text": "[3] This implies that he held a previous citizenship, which was that of the Dominion of India."}, "D2S18": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1731, "end": 1745, "text": "**Conclusion**"}, "D2S19": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1747, "end": 1858, "text": "Based on the evidence presented, it is clear that Rangaswamy Srinivasan was a citizen of the Dominion of India."}, "D2S20": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1859, "end": 2003, "text": "Born in 1929, during the British Raj, Srinivasan automatically became a citizen of the Dominion of India when India gained independence in 1947."}, "D2S21": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2004, "end": 2137, "text": "His citizenship of the Dominion of India is supported by credible sources, including his own statements and biographical information."}, "D2S22": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2138, "end": 2152, "text": "**References**"}, "D2S23": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2154, "end": 2188, "text": "[1] Indian Independence Act, 1947."}, "D2S24": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2189, "end": 2196, "text": "(1947)."}}, "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d1", "card_id": "d1:c1", "entity": "Rangaswamy Srinivasan", "scope": "citizenship", "claim": "Rangaswamy Srinivasan is a citizen of the United States.", "answer": "United States", "quote": "Srinivasan's family remained in Yugoslavia until 1965, when they moved to the United States, where Srinivasan would go on to pursue his education and build a successful career in engineering.", "original_document_number": 1}], "current_answers": ["United States", "Dominion of India", "India"], "candidate_answers": [{"candidate_id": "R0", "answer": "United States", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R1", "answer": "Dominion of India", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R2", "answer": "India", "origin": "coverage_addition"}], "requested_slot_hint": "other"}
